{"name":"Realm of the Underworld","hex":"#114411","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"realm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A territory or state, as ruled by an absolute authority, especially by a king; a kingdom. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n\n An otherworldly dimension or domain — magical, ethereal, or otherwise.\n The spiritual state of which God is the head; the Kingdom of Heaven.","An otherworldly dimension or domain — magical, ethereal, or otherwise."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/realm"},{"term":"underworld","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The world of the dead, located underneath the world of the living; the afterlife.","That part of society that is engaged in crime or vice, and particularly those involved in organized crime."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underworld"}],"entries":[{"title":"Realm","blocks":[{"text":"A realm is a community or territory over which a sovereign rules. The term is commonly used to describe a monarchical or dynastic state. A realm may also be a subdivision within an empire, if it has its own monarch, e.g. the German Empire."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Realm","wikidata":"Q1250464"},{"title":"Underworld","blocks":[{"text":"The underworld, also known as the netherworld or hell, is the supernatural world of the dead in various religious traditions and myths, located below the world of the living. Chthonic is the technical adjective for things of the underworld."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Jan_Brueghel_the_Younger_-_Juno_in_the_Underworld%2C_1626-1630.jpg/330px-Jan_Brueghel_the_Younger_-_Juno_in_the_Underworld%2C_1626-1630.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Underworld","wikidata":"Q154365"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Portuguese_empire_1800.png/500px-Po